// Clang module map for GenesisBlockDB.xcframework's binaryTarget consumers.
//
// GenesisBlockDB.xcframework wraps a plain C static library + genesisdb.h —
// with no module map, Swift's `import GenesisBlockDB` cannot resolve against
// it (found on mobile-acceptance/ios's ios-acceptance-test CI job: builds
// failed with "unable to resolve module dependency: 'GenesisBlockDB'" even
// after the zip/scheme-name fixes were in place). ios/genesisdb sidesteps
// this by declaring its own local CGenesisDBFFI system-library target with
// its own module map (see ios/genesisdb/Sources/CGenesisDBFFI/module.modulemap)
// — but a binaryTarget consumer (mobile-acceptance/ios, and any future real
// external consumer of the published xcframework) has no such local target
// to lean on, so the module map has to live inside the xcframework itself.
//
// `xcodebuild -create-xcframework -headers include/` (see
// .github/workflows/mobile-build.yml's ios-xcframework job) copies this
// entire directory — this file included — into each library slice's
// Headers/ folder, which is the documented way to make an xcframework's C
// library importable as a Clang module from Swift. The module name here
// (GenesisBlockDB) must match Package.swift's `.binaryTarget(name:
// "GenesisBlockDB", ...)` for `import GenesisBlockDB` to resolve.
module GenesisBlockDB {
    header "genesisdb.h"
    export *
}
